  "implemented": [
    "Single identity-owned personal workspace provisioning port reused by registration, login repair and current/default workspace resolution",
    "Account-row serialization; tenant, owner membership, baseline directory and READY state in one transaction",
    "Existing personal workspaces require explicit legacy adoption; login cannot auto-grant missing historical rights",
    "Historical owner membership is repaired in place without issuing role grants or synchronizing platform definitions",
    "Unique personal workspace names with Unicode code-point length handling",
    "Trusted system-account startup path separated from ordinary registration, with no HTTP/RPC skip flag and no request-context availability",
    "Seed account and configured root identity committed in the same transaction; existing bootstrap contribution identity/version preserved",
    "Bootstrap lookup does not provision workspaces or swallow database failures",
    "Platform-account HTTP setup failures retain stable namespaced errors and localized message keys"
  ],
